UPDATE companies SET description='Ohio Steel Industries was founded in 1958 in Columbus, Ohio, when a single employee began operating a structural steel fabrication shop in a 25,000-square-foot facility serving central Ohio. The company has since expanded to multiple locations totaling more than 300,000 square feet and serves customers worldwide.

The business operates through three divisions. The Manufacturing Division provides contract fabrication of lawn and garden riding mower attachments, utility trailers, loading ramps, and display merchandising, using processes that include stamping, welding, bending, cutting, forming, powder coating, packaging, and shipping. OSI Plastics, an ISO 9001:2015-registered division, produces extruded plastic profiles for utilities, telecommunications firms, and other large enterprises across the United States and Europe. The Structural Steel Division, housed in a 120,000-square-foot plant in Pataskala, fabricates, furnishes, and erects structural steel for buildings and bridges and holds AISC certification for standard, simply supported, and major bridge structures.

Customers range from retail mass merchants and OEM lawn-and-garden manufacturers to distributors, dealers, public utilities, and telecommunications companies. The structural division serves the construction sector, while the plastics division supplies large publicly traded companies. Products are shipped globally, with a particular presence in the U.S. and European markets.

The company states its commitments as providing a safe workplace, exceeding customer expectations in quality and delivery, expanding its market through research and development, developing and retaining its workforce, and creating jobs in its community. Its differentiators include AISC-certified structural fabrication, ISO 9001:2015 registration for plastics, and full-service metal fabrication under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AISC Certification (Standard for Steel Building Structures, Simply Steel Bridges, Major Steel Bridges)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural Steel Fabrication", "Plastic Extrusion", "Contract Manufacturing", "Stamping", "Welding", "Bending", "Cutting", "Forming", "Powder Coating", "Packaging", "Shipping", "Product Assembly", "Riding Mower Attachment Manufacturing", "Utility Trailer Fabrication", "Loading Ramp Fabrication", "Display Merchandising Fabrication", "Plastic Profile Extrusion", "Building Steel Fabrication", "Bridge Steel Fabrication", "Steel Erection", "Engineering and Customization"], "industries": ["Lawn & Garden", "Retail (Mass Merchants)", "OEM Lawn & Garden Manufacturing", "Distribution & Dealers", "Public Utilities", "Telecommunications", "Construction (Buildings & Bridges)", "Contract Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Steel (sheet and tubular)", "Plastic resins"], "equipment": ["Powder coating lines", "Plastic extrusion lines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC-certified structural steel fabrication for buildings and bridges", "ISO 9001:2015 registered plastic extrusion division", "Full-service steel fabrication (stamping, welding, forming, powder coating, packaging) in-house", "Over 300,000 sq ft across multiple facilities", "Global shipping to retail, OEM, utility, and construction markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958, one employee, structural steel fabricator, 25,000 sq ft Columbus facility -> /about-us", "Now operates multiple facilities >300,000 sq ft worldwide -> /about-us", "Three divisions: Manufacturing, OSI Plastics, Structural Steel -> /about-us", "Manufacturing Division: contract manufacturing, lawn & garden attachments, utility trailers, loading ramps, display merchandising; processes: stamping, welding, bending, cutting, forming, powder coating, packaging, shipping -> /about-us", "OSI Plastics: ISO 9001:2015 registered, extruded plastic products for utilities, telecommunications, large publicly traded companies; US and Europe -> /about-us", "Structural Steel Division: AISC certified, fabricates/furnishes/erects structural steel for buildings and bridges; 120,000 sq ft facility in Pataskala -> /about-us", "Company commitments: safe workplace, exceed customer expectations, expand marketplace via R&D, develop/retain workforce, create jobs -> /about-us", "General managers: Ken Hoffmann (Manufacturing), Jon Van Gundy (OSI Plastics), Mike Miller (Structural Steel) -> /about-us", "Headquarters: 2575 Ferris Road, Columbus OH 43224 -> /, /about-us", "Founded year 1958 -> db", "Certifications: ISO9001 (db), ISO 9001:2015 (page), AISC (page) -> db, /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ohio-steel-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Orion Plastics Inc. was founded in 2001 in Compton, California, as a custom manufacturer of polyethylene bags, sheeting, and tubing. The company operates from a single location in Compton with several extrusion lines.

The company produces a wide range of polyethylene products including bags (box liners, bin liners, pallet covers, hazardous waste bags, furniture and mattress bags), sheeting (agricultural, mulch film, shrink bundling, anti-static), and tubing (anti-static, shrink, perforated, continuous on roll). Its extrusion lines are capable of producing millions of pounds of product annually, supported by printing capabilities (1C-2S and 2C-1S) and converting equipment for loose bags, roll bags, and gusseted configurations up to 144 inches wide. Gauges run up to 0.010 inch, with standard 3-inch ID cores and roll diameters from 8 to 30 inches.

Orion serves customers in food processing (FDA compliant and SQF certified), agriculture, construction, hazardous waste management, asbestos abatement, furniture and bedding, and textile industries. Specific product examples include FDA-compliant box liners, agricultural mulch film, hazardous waste bags, asbestos removal bags, and furniture and mattress bags.

The company emphasizes flexibility without sacrificing dependability, offering custom sizing, venting options, slip levels, and leak-proof seals. Its FDA compliance and SQF certification support food-contact applications.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA COMPLIANT','SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polyethylene extrusion (bags, sheeting, tubing)", "Flexographic printing (1C-2S, 2C-1S)", "Bag converting (loose bags, bags on rolls, gusseted bags)", "Custom width sizing (8\" to 120\")", "Center slit film and centerfold sheeting (opening to 288\")", "Gauge control up to 0.010 inch", "Standard 3\" ID cores", "Roll diameter 8\" to 30\"", "Color options (tint, heavy tint, opaque)", "Vent holes (1/4\" or 3/8\" full vents, butterfly vents)", "Slip level control (low, medium, high)", "Leak proof seals", "Form/fill/seal film production", "Shrink bundle film production", "Grizzly film production", "Anti-static additive incorporation", "Perforated tubing", "Continuous tubing on a roll"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Polyethylene"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Millions of pounds annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Several extrusion lines producing millions of pounds annually", "Flexibility without sacrificing dependability (company statement)", "FDA compliant and SQF certified for food contact", "Printing capabilities: 1C-2S and 2C-1S", "Wide range of bag sizes and configurations (loose, roll, gusseted up to 144\")"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> db", "Headquarters: Compton, California -> db", "Custom manufacturer of polyethylene bags, sheeting, tubing -> /", "Several extrusion lines capable of millions of pounds annually -> /", "FDA compliant and SQF certified -> /, db", "Printing capabilities 1C-2S & 2C-1S -> /capabilities", "Bag sizes: loose 18-98\", on rolls 18-98\", gusseted up to 144\" -> /capabilities", "Gauges up to .010 -> /capabilities", "Standard 3\" ID cores, roll diameter 8-30\" -> /capabilities", "Color options, vent holes, sli