UPDATE companies SET description='Pegasus Food Group was founded in 1998 in Los Angeles, California as a family business. After two decades of growth, the company relocated its operations to Rockwall, Texas in 2018 to support expanded production capacity. The business began with a focus on culinary creativity and has since evolved into a full-service co-manufacturer of frozen appetizers, snacks, and meal solutions.

Today the company operates a 135,000-square-foot SQF-certified USDA facility in Rockwall equipped with seven production lines. Capabilities include dough extrusion and co-extrusion, automated and hand-rolled forming, inline frying and baking, batter and breading, ammonia-based freezing, and X-ray inspection. An in-house culinary R&D team supports product development from ideation through commercialization, leveraging equipment such as Rheon and Vemag systems. The facility produces a range of frozen items including rangoon scoops, empanadas, egg rolls, burritos, poppers, bulk fillings, and desserts.

Pegasus serves national consumer brands, supermarket retailers, club stores, quick-service and casual-dining restaurant chains, and foodservice distributors. It also manages private-label programs for major grocery and club channels and markets its own brands, By the Bite and The Perfect Bite Co. Client relationships are often confidential; testimonials reference retail, foodservice, and emerging-brand partners who value the company’s responsiveness and consistency at scale.

The company positions itself on a combination of scale and agility: a large certified facility paired with a “nimble” operating model that emphasizes quick response, rapid changeover, and fast time-to-market.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Co-manufacturing", "Private label manufacturing", "Retail private label solutions", "QSR and foodservice product development", "Culinary R&D and product development", "Extrusion and co-extrusion", "Dough extrusion and forming", "Automated forming", "Hand-rolled forming", "Inline frying", "Baking", "Batter and breading", "Ammonia-based freezing", "X-ray inspection", "Packaging (various sizes, shapes, coatings)", "Rheon technology", "Vemag technology"], "industries": ["National consumer brands", "Supermarket retailers", "Club retailers", "Quick-service restaurants (QSR)", "Casual dining restaurants", "Foodservice distributors", "Private label programs", "Emerging food brands"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Rheon technology", "Vemag technology", "X-ray inspection systems", "Ammonia-based freezing systems", "Dough extrusion and forming systems", "Inline frying systems", "Bakery ovens", "Batter and breading equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["135,000 sq ft SQF-certified frozen USDA facility in Rockwall, Texas", "In-house culinary R&D team taking products from ideation to commercialization", "Seven production lines with inline frying, baking, extrusion, forming, and X-ray inspection", "Nimble operations: quick response, adaptability, and fast time-to-market", "Capacity for growth through automation investment and production efficiencies"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 in Los Angeles as family business -> /about-us", "Relocated to Rockwall, Texas in 2018 -> /about-us", "135,000 sq ft manufacturing facility in Rockwall, Texas -> /about-us", "SQF certified frozen USDA facility -> /about-us", "7 production lines with fryers, ovens, extrusion, forming, X-ray inspection -> /about-us", "In-house culinary R&D team -> /about-us", "Co-manufacturing, private label, QSR/foodservice, retail expertise -> /", "Owned brands: By the Bite and The Perfect Bite Co. -> /", "Industries: national supermarket chains, club retailers, QSR, casual dining, foodservice distributors, private label programs -> /", "Leadership team: David Higgs (CEO), Vanessa Thanos (CCO), Steven Betrisey (VP Sales), Mike Erickson (CFO), Sheila Edwards (Sr. Director Supply Chain), Mayra Romero (Director SIOP) -> /about-us", "Values: safety, bravery, momentum, continuous improvement, respect, empowerment, pursue best over easiest -> /about-us", "Equipment: Rheon, Vemag, X-ray, ammonia freezing, dough extrusion/forming, inline frying, bakery, batter/breading -> /about-us", "Founded year 1998 from database -> db", "HQ Rockwall, Texas from database -> db", "Certifications SQF from database -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pegasus-foods-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pennsylvania Transformer Technology (PTT) traces its roots to 1929 in Canonsburg, Pennsylvania, where the company now occupies a 1-million-square-foot, 18-building campus on 90 acres — a site that previously housed McGraw-Edison and Cooper Power Systems transformer operations.

PTT designs and manufactures oil-filled power transformers ranging from 500 kVA to 750 MVA with voltage ratings through 765 kV, including generator step-up, autotransformers, pad-mount, unit substation, mobile, and specialty industrial transformers. The Canonsburg facility features North America’s largest GEORG automatic core cutting and stacking line, a 200,000-square-foot tank fabrication bay, 500-ton lifting capacity, and test capability to 765 kV/2400 kV BIL. Beyond new builds, the Power Solutions division provides full lifecycle services: field installation, preventive maintenance, oil processing, repairs, refurbishment, engineering studies (loading, cooling, condition assessment, life extension, stray flux), and authorized replacement parts for load tap changers and circuit breakers from legacy brands such as McGraw-Edison, Cooper Power, and Federal Pacific. The Green Core division handles transformer decommissioning and recycling nationwide.

The company serves electric utilities, data centers, renewable energy developers (solar, wind), battery energy storage systems (BESS), heavy industrial manufacturing, and power generation. Its transformers are deployed in utility substations, hyperscale data centers, and grid-integration projects for renewables and storage.

PTT emphasizes its nearly 100 years of continuous transformer engineering, dual U.S. production sites, ISO 9001:2015 with Design certification, and the backing of Quanta Services as factors that differentiate it from overseas suppliers and enable support for large-scale infrastructure projects.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015 with Design']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power transformer manufacturing (500 kVA \u2013 750 MVA, through 765 kV)", "Pad-mount transformer manufacturing", "Substation/unit substation transformer manufacturing", "Mobile transformer manufacturing", "Specialty transformer manufacturing (GSU, autotransformers, zig-zag, series-multiple, furnace, transit)", "Shunt reactor manufacturing (up to 150 MVAr, through 765 kV)", "Coil winding", "Core fabrication (GEORG automatic core cutting and stacking)", "Tank fabrication", "High-voltage testing (765 kV, 2400 kV BIL)", "Field installation services", "Preventive maintenance", "Oil processing (mineral and natural ester fluids)", "Transformer repair and refurbishment", "Equipment upgrades and retrofits", "Engineering studies (loading, cooling, condition assessment, life extension, stray flux)", "Load tap changer parts supply (authorized for McGraw-Edison, Cooper Power, PTT)", "Circuit breaker parts supply (authorized for McGraw-Edison, Cooper Power, Federal Pacific, Pennsylvania Breaker)", "Reverse engineering", "Turn-key support", "Control upgrades", "Reconditioning services", "Transformer decommissioning and recycling (Green Core)", "Field service engineering"], "industries": ["Electric Utilities", "Data Centers", "Renewable Energy", "Battery Energy Storage Systems (BESS)", "Heavy Industrial Manufacturing", "Power Generation", "Transit"], "materials": ["Mineral oil", "Natural ester fluids", "Copper windings", "Aluminum windings"], "equipment": ["GEORG Automatic Core Cutting and Stacking Line", "200,000 sq ft Tank Fabrication Bay", "500-ton lifting capacity", "765 kV / 2400 kV BIL test capabi