UPDATE companies SET description='Polyzen LLC was founded in 1991 by polymer chemist Tilak M. Shah in Apex, North Carolina, to serve as a contract developer and supplier for medical device OEMs and start-ups. Now part of the Solesis family of companies—alongside Secant Group, SanaVita Medical, and Charter Medical—Polyzen operates a 75,000-square-foot facility near the Raleigh-Durham research corridor.

The company develops and manufactures customized polymer-based materials, films, components, and finished assemblies for medical devices. Its processing capabilities span elastomer and silicone formulation, specialty film extrusion, barrier films and laminates, dip molding and coating, stent and wire coatings, low- and high-pressure balloon production, multi-layer balloons, catheter fabrication and assembly, lay-flat sheathes and tubing, thin-film welding, and thermoforming. Polyzen supports projects from prototype through full-scale production, offering validation, packaging, and sterilization management under one roof.

Polyzen serves the medical device and life sciences sectors, working with entrepreneurial start-ups as well as major OEMs developing Class I, II, and III devices. Its quality system complies with FDA cGMP (21 CFR Part 820), ISO 13485:2016, ISO 9001:2015, and Japanese MHLW requirements, enabling global supply.

The firm’s stated mission is to accelerate product realization by acting as an extension of customers’ engineering and manufacturing teams. Core principles emphasize urgency in turning ideas into solutions, attention to detail in quality and sustainability, and creating value for patients. Integrated R&D with sister companies further expands its material science and processing expertise.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2015','FDA Registered (QSR 21, CFR Part 820)','GMP Compliant for Phase 1 Investigational Drug/Device Combination Products','Japan MHLW Ministerial Ordinal 169']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polymer material formulation and consultation", "Specialty film extrusion", "Barrier films and laminates", "Dip molding and coating", "Coatings for stents, wires, and instruments", "Low-pressure compliant balloon manufacturing", "High-pressure balloon manufacturing", "Multi-layer balloon manufacturing", "Catheter fabrication and assembly", "Lay-flat sheathes and tubing", "Thin film welding", "Thermoforming", "Sheet and tube extrusion", "Molding", "Product development and optimization", "Design for manufacturability", "Prototyping to full-scale manufacturing", "Validation, packaging, and sterilization management", "Testing and inspection", "Regulatory compliance support"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Life Sciences"], "materials": ["Elastomers", "Silicone", "Specialty Films", "Barrier Films", "Laminates", "Medical-Grade Polymers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end polymer services from material formulation to finished device assembly", "Integrated R&D with sister companies Secant Group, SanaVita Medical, Charter Medical", "ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certified, FDA registered, GMP compliant for combination products", "75,000 sq. ft. facility with company-owned equipment and in-house validation capabilities", "Supports Class I, II, and III 