UPDATE companies SET description='Powell Industries was founded in 1947 by William E. Powell in Houston, Texas, initially as a metal-working shop serving the local petrochemical industry. The company developed the Power Control Room concept in 1968 for a Union Carbide project in Puerto Rico, marking an early move into integrated electrical infrastructure.

Today Powell operates globally with over 1,000 employees, designing and manufacturing low- and medium-voltage switchgear, motor control centers, transformers, and power control rooms. Its portfolio includes ANSI metal-clad and metal-enclosed switchgear, IEC-rated switchgear, and the PowlVac Series 5 circuit breaker, supported by custom engineering, centralized project management, and integrated package solutions.

The company serves oil and gas refining, offshore production, petrochemical plants, pipelines, data centers, electric utilities, traction power, renewables, mining and metals, commercial construction, pulp and paper, and government agencies. It also lists power utilities and general industrial markets among its core sectors.

Powell distinguishes itself through a single-source model that combines centralized engineering and project management with global factory and service locations, an approach rooted in its original mission to support complex electrical infrastructure needs. The company emphasizes a safety-first culture and a "can-do" attitude toward solving customer challenges.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Switchgear manufacturing", "Motor control center assembly", "Transformer manufacturing", "Power control room integration", "Custom engineered solutions", "Project management", "Engineering services", "Integrated package solutions", "ANSI metal-clad switchgear production", "ANSI metal-enclosed switchgear production", "IEC switchgear production", "PowlVac circuit breaker manufacturing"], "industries": ["Oil and Gas Refining", "Offshore Oil and Gas Production", "Petrochemical", "Pipelines", "Data Centers", "Electric Utilities", "Traction Power", "Renewables", "Mining and Metals", "Commercial", "Pulp and Paper", "Government", "Power Utilities", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["PowlVac Series 5 Circuit Breaker"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source supplier for project execution and delivery", "Centralized engineering and project management", "Global factory and service locations", "Custom engineered solutions tailored to customer needs", "Safety-focused culture (Powered By Safety\u2122)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1947 by William E. Powell in Houston, Texas -> /about", "Started as metal-working shop for petrochemical facilities -> /about", "Developed Power Control Room concept in 1968 for Union Carbide -> /about", "Employee count 1000+ -> db", "Products: low- and medium-voltage switchgear, motor control centers, transformers, power control rooms -> db, /", "ANSI metal-clad and metal-enclosed switchgear, IEC switchgear -> /", "PowlVac Series 5 circuit breaker -> /", "Industries served: oil and g