UPDATE companies SET description='Praxis Packaging was founded in 1989 in Grand Rapids, Michigan, as a contract packaging provider for the life sciences and consumer health sectors. The company operates cGMP-compliant, DEA-registered (Schedules III-V) facilities offering primary solid dose packaging — bottling and blistering — along with liquid filling for creams, pastes, lotions, and oils. Secondary packaging services include labeling, cartoning, bundling, kitting, clamshell blistering, and stretch carding. Praxis also provides DSCSA serialization with aggregation and EPCIS integration, rework and inspection, and cGMP cold chain storage, with 24/7 operations available for time-sensitive projects.

The company serves pharmaceutical, biotech, animal health, medical device, nutritional, and personal care markets. Customers include Rx and OTC pharmaceutical manufacturers, biotech firms requiring vial labeling and complex kitting, medical device companies needing precision kitting and domestic production of NIOSH-approved surgical N95 respirators, animal health brands, nutritional supplement companies, and personal care brands for cosmetics, skin care, and oral hygiene products.

Praxis emphasizes quality, innovation, and customer success as differentiators, positioning itself as a strategic partner for speed to market through flexibility, responsiveness, and agility. Its 35-plus years of experience, comprehensive quality systems, and domestic manufacturing capabilities for NIOSH-approved respirators are cited as foundations for reliability.', certifications=ARRAY['cGMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Primary solid dose bottling", "Primary solid dose blistering", "Liquid filling (liquid, cream, paste, lotion, oils)", "Secondary packaging (labeling, cartoning, bundling)", "Kitting and assembly", "Clamshell blistering", "Stretch carding", "DSCSA serialization", "Serialization aggregation (parent-child)", "EPCIS integration", "Rework and inspection", "Cold chain storage", "Contract packaging for medical devices", "N95 respirator manufacturing (NIOSH-approved)"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Biotech", "Animal health", "Medical device", "Nutritional", "Personal care"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small projects to large production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["DEA-registered for Schedule III-V controlled substances", "24/7 operations available for time-sensitive projects", "DSCSA serialization with EPCIS integration and aggregation", "cGMP cold chain storage facilities", "Domestic manufacturing of NIOSH-approved surgical N95 respirators"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 in Grand Rapids, Michigan -> /", "cGMP-compliant, DEA-registered (Schedules III-V) facilities -> /", "Primary solid dose bottling and blistering -> /", "Liquid filling for creams, pastes, liquids -> /", "Secondary packaging: labeling, cartoning, bundling, kitting, clamshell, stretch carding -> /", "DSCSA serialization with aggregation and EPCIS integration -> /", "Rework and inspection services -> /", "24/7 operations for time-sensitive projects -> /", "cGMP cold chain storage -> /", "Serves pharmaceutical, biotech, animal healt