UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Textiles is headquartered in Totowa, New Jersey. The company traces its roots to 1987 when Peter Longo founded Precision Custom Coatings as a supplier of interlinings to apparel distributors and fabric wholesalers. Longo remains chairman. Scott Tesser, now chief executive officer and co-owner, joined the business after the apparel trade moved offshore and built an Asia-based supply model for customers. In 2000 Longo and Tesser bought back the company from a private-equity owner and renamed it Precision Textiles to pursue markets beyond apparel.

Today the firm designs, produces and globally distributes fire-retardant nonwovens, laminates, coated fabrics and specialty fibers from a 210,000-square-foot headquarters that houses a state-of-the-art laboratory, factory and warehouse. Four additional U.S. warehouses and three overseas joint-venture warehouses extend its reach. An in-house R&D team operates around the clock to develop and lab-test solutions for bedding, automotive and healthcare applications.

Customers include mattress and sleep-product manufacturers, automotive OEMs and tier suppliers, and healthcare product makers. In the automotive sector the company has supplied materials for speaker components, upholstery liners, dashboard and door-panel insulation, and headliners. For bedding it provides a range of glass-free flame-barrier products such as ECOFLEX, IQFit Natural and the GOTS-certified PureLoft wool barrier.

The shift into bedding was driven by the 2004 federal open-flame mattress standard. Precision Textiles emphasizes environmentally conscious methods: solar panels at its factory, GOTS-certified organic wool, and a portfolio of recyclable, non-allergenic fibers. Its Precision Cares program donates bedding and furniture to non-profits serving children, veterans and domestic-abuse survivors.', certifications=ARRAY['GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard)','Wool Integrity Program','PGG Wrightson Wool Integrity Program']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Nonwoven manufacturing", "Lamination", "Fabric coating", "Fire retardant treatment", "Quilting fiber production", "FR barrier fabrication", "Research and development", "Laboratory testing", "Global warehousing and distribution", "Product design and engineering", "Sustainable material sourcing", "Custom formulation"], "industries": ["Bedding", "Automotive", "Healthcare", "Consumer products", "Mattress and sleep products", "Apparel"], "materials": ["Organic wool fiber (GOTS-certified)", "Conjugated spiral crimp pillow fill", "Bicomponent polyester", "Inherent FR rayon", "Sustainable cotton", "Glass-free FR materials", "Para-aramid free fibers", "Antimony free fibers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house R&D laboratory with 24/7 testing capability", "Global network of owned and joint-venture warehouses", "Proprietary eco-friendly FR product lines (ECOLOFT, ECOFLEX, IQFit Natural, PureLoft)", "GOTS-certified organic wool and other sustainable material certifications", "Collaborative product development model with customers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Totowa, New Jersey -> /about-us", "Founded 1987 as Precision Custom Coatings by Peter Longo -> /about-us", "Scott Tesser joined, established Asia business model -> /about-us", "Longo and Tesser acquired company in 2000 -> /about-us", "210,000-square-foot HQ with lab, factory, warehouse -> /about-us", "Four U.S. wareho