UPDATE companies SET description='Production Sciences, Inc. has operated from Chestertown, Maryland since its founding in June 1989. The company remains at its original location on Dixon Drive, conducting all manufacturing domestically.

The firm produces soft plastic components through dip molding, dip coating, and plastisol casting. Dip molding creates connectors, caps, and sleeves by dipping heated metal forms into liquid plastisol, curing, and stripping the finished part. Dip coating applies protective or aesthetic plastisol layers onto customer-supplied metal parts such as brackets, hooks, and spring latches. Plastisol casting pours liquid material into metal molds to form solid objects, which can be die-cut and given adhesive backings for marker applications. An onsite machine shop builds and iterates tooling, enabling concept-to-sample turnaround in as little as one week. Modeling services use SolidWorks to generate 2D drawings and 3D models from customer concepts or existing files. The company states it handles components of all quantities and physical sizes, scaling from prototype to full production runs.

Industrial clients also use the service for protective coatings and colored components. Specific examples cited include elongated caps for medical devices, coated spring latches, and protective brackets.

The onsite tooling capability is presented as a key enabler for rapid prototyping and cost-effective scaling.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dip molding", "Dip coating", "Plastisol casting", "SolidWorks 2D/3D modeling", "Rapid prototyping", "Tooling fabrication", "Plastisol material selection", "Protective coating for metal components", "Aesthetic coating for metal components", "Adhesive marker fabrication"], "industries": ["Medical", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Plastisol (PVC-based)", "Phthalate-free plastisol", "Medical-grade transparent plastisol", "Opaque colored plastisol", "Radiopaque compound additives", "Scent additives"], "equipment": ["Onsite machine shop", "SolidWorks CAD software"], "volume": "Prototype to full production volumes", "lead_time": "As little as one week for prototypes", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded June 1989, located Chestertown, MD -> /", "All manufacturing in USA at Chestertown -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Dip molding, dip coating, plastisol casting processes -> /", "Onsite machine shop for tooling -> /", "Rapid prototyping: concept to sample in as little as one week -> /", "SolidWorks modeling services -> /", "Medical industry focus, clean non-sterile, radiopaque compounds -> /", "Industrial applications: opaque colored for industrial -> /", "Components of all quantities and sizes -> /", "Phthalate-free options -> /", "Materials: transparent medical-grade, opaque colored, additives -> /", "Examples: elongated cap for medical device, coated spring latch, protective bracket -> /", "Headquarters: 127 Dixon Drive, Chestertown, MD 21620 -> /", "Founded year 1989 from db -> db", "Certifications ISO9001 from db -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='production-science-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Proterial Cable America, Inc. traces its roots to 1986 when Hitachi Cable America established a manufacturing facility in Manchester, New Hampshire. The company, now a subsidiary of Proterial Ltd. (formerly Hitachi Metals), rebranded to its current name as part of a global corporate identity shift. From its New Hampshire headquarters, the business has expanded to eight manufacturing sites worldwide, including locations in Indiana, Mexico, Rhode Island, and Connecticut.

The company operates through three divisions. The Performance Cable Systems & Materials Division produces copper and fiber optic communication cables and assemblies supporting Ethernet, video, Power over Ethernet, HDMI, and InfiniBand applications. The Automotive Products Division supplies original equipment manufacturers and Tier 1 suppliers with power cable harnesses for electric and hybrid vehicles, brake hoses, electronic parking brake harnesses, wheel speed sensors, and torque sensors. The High Performance Medical Solutions Division, certified to ISO 13485:2016, provides complex catheter tubing, braided and high-pressure braided tubing, secondary operations, medical machining, fabrication, 3D additive manufacturing, cable assemblies, and full device assembly for products such as PICC catheters, introducer sheaths, fluid transport tubing, ultrasound devices, endoscopic camera catheters, and advanced diagnostic or surgical catheters. The combined facilities offer both high-volume production and rapid prototyping capabilities.

Proterial Cable America serves four primary sectors: data communications OEMs requiring high-performance connectivity; medical device OEMs needing precision extrusion and assembly; automotive OEMs and major Tier 1s sourcing brake and sensor systems; and defense contractors requiring ITAR-compliant manufacturing.

The company emphasizes a "Professional, Proactive, Progressive" approach, highlighting long-term customer relationships, rigorous quality control under ISO 9001:2015, and a safety-first culture across all divisions. Its engineering team of 43 specialists works to integrate design, compliance, and manufacturing to accelerate customer innovation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Copper communication cable manufacturing", "Fiber optic cable manufacturing", "Cable assembly (Ethernet, video, PoE, HDMI, InfiniBand)", "Medical extrusion (custom tubing and wire components)", "High-pressure braided tubing production", "Medical secondary operations", "Medical machining and fabrication", "3D additive manufacturing for medical devices", "Medical cable assembly", "Full medical device assembly", "Automotive power cable harness manufacturing (EV/hybrid)", "Brake hose manufacturing", "Electronic parking brake harness assembly", "Wheel speed sensor manufacturing", "Torque sensor manufacturing", "Custom brake system production", "Sensing and power product manufacturing", "High-volume production", "Low-volume and prototype manufacturing", "Custom extrusion quoting service", "Medical research and development"], "industries": ["Data Communications", "Medical Devices", "Automotive", "Defense"], "materials": ["Copper", "Fiber optic", "Medical-grade tubing polymers", "Automotive brake hose compounds", "Wire harness insulation materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 in Manchester, NH -> db", "Formerly Hitachi Cable America, rebranded to Proterial Cable America -> /about", "Subsidiary of Proterial Ltd. (formerly Hitachi Metals) -> /about", "Eight manufacturing facilities globally -> /", "Three divisions: Performance Cable Systems & Materials, Automotive Products, High Performance Medical Solutions -> /about", "Performance Cable Systems facility in Manchester since 1986 -> /about", "Automotive facilities in Indiana and Mexico -> /about", "Medical division facilities in Rhode Island, Connecticut, New Hampshire -> /about", "43 specialized engineers across divisions -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about", "ITAR compliant -> /, /about, db", "Medical division ISO 13485:2016 compliant -> /about", "Copper and fiber optic communication cables for Ethernet, video, PoE, HDMI, InfiniBand -> /about", "Automotive products: power cable harnesses for EV/hybrid, brake hoses, electronic parking brake harnesses, wheel speed sensors, torque sensors -> /about, /", "Medical products: catheter tubing, braided tubing, high-pressure braided tubing, secondary operations, medical machining, fabrication, 3D additive manufacturing, cable assemblies, full device assembly -> /about", "Medical examples: PICC catheters, introducer sheaths, fluid transport tubing, ultrasound devices, endoscopic camera catheters, diagnostic/surgical catheters -> /about", "Industries served: Data Communications, Medical, Automotive, Defense -> /, /about", "High and low volume capabilities -> /, db", "Rapid manufacturing for low or prototype runs -> /", "Samples available in 1m increments up to 5m -> /", "Quotes available in 100m increments -> /", "Professional, Proactive, Progressive philosophy -> /", "Relationships That Last, Dedication to Engineering Perfection, Always Safety-First -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='proterial-cable-america-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Protoline Inc. was founded in 1987 by Paresh Jasani and Hitesh Jasani in Houston, Texas. The minority-owned company began after the founders gained experience in the printed circuit board manufacturing business.

The company operates a 20,000-square-foot facility certified to ISO 9001:2008, UL 94 V-0, and ITAR, capable of processing more than 1,000 18-by-24-inch panels per day. It produces single-sided, double-sided, and multilayer boards up to 20 layers, using substrates such as FR-4, FR-5, polyimide, and Teflon. Services include PCB layout and design, ECAD, design-for-manufacturability review, through-hole and surface-mount assembly, rigid-flex and flexible circuits, electrical testing, and full turnkey contract manufacturing with wire harness and box-build options. Quick-turn orders can ship in one to ten days, while standard lead time is about three weeks.

Protoline serves a range of industries including contract manufacturing, oil and gas, telecommunications, medical devices, data processing, recorders, controllers, audio, video, and aerospace.

The founders emphasize quality, on-time delivery, and competitive pricing, with a focus on design-to-manufacture support to avoid production issues.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008','UL 94 V-0','RoHS Compliance','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Single-sided PCB", "Double-sided PCB", "Multi-layer PCB (up to 20 layers)", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT)", "Through-hole PCB", "Rigid-flex PCB", "Flexible circuits", "PCB layout and design", "ECAD PCB design", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Electrical testing", "Scoring", "Scanning", "Reverse engineering", "Contract manufacturing (turnkey)", "Wire and cable harness assembly", "Box build assembly", "Quick turn delivery (1-10 days)", "Standard delivery (3 weeks)"], "industries": ["Contract manufacturing", "Oil and gas", "Telecommunications", "Medical devices", "Data processing", "Recorders", "Controllers", "Audio", "Video", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["FR-4", "FR-5", "CEM", "Polyimide", "Arlon", "Rogers", "Microwave", "Teflon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to medium production; up to 20-layer boards; capacity over 1,000 18x24 panels per day", "lead_time": "Quick turn: 1-10 days; Standard delivery: 3 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick-turn delivery in 1\u201310 days", "Facility capacity over 1,000 panels per day", "Up to 20-layer board capability", "Design-for-manufacturability (DFM) support", "Minority-owned and ITAR-registered"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 by Paresh and Hitesh Jasani -> /", "Houston, Texas headquarters -> db", "20,000 sq ft facility -> /", "Capacity 1,000 panels/day -> /", "Up to 20-layer boards -> /", "ISO 9001:2008 certified -> /capabilities", "UL 94 V-0 -> /capabilities", "ITAR registered -> /capabilities", "Minority-owned -> /", "Industries served: contract manufacturing, oil & gas, telecommunication, medical, data processing, recorders, controllers, audio, video, aerospace -> /", "Quick turn 1-10 days -> /capabilities", "Standard delivery 3 weeks -> /cap