UPDATE companies SET description='Puritan Medical Products, founded in 1919 as Hardwood Products Company, operates from Guilford, Maine. The family-owned business rebranded to Puritan Medical Products Company I, LP in January 2023. It began producing single-use items from Northern white birch and evolved into a specialized manufacturer of swabs and specimen collection devices.

The company runs three manufacturing facilities in Maine — Guilford and two in Pittsfield — where it produces swabs, applicators, and single-use medical devices. Capabilities include flocked swab production, custom fill of transport media, an on-site microbiology lab staffed with microbiologists, a state-of-the-art print shop for labeling and packaging, and full R&D prototyping. The Guilford plant uses 100% renewable energy from wood process waste; overall facilities achieve 35% renewable energy. Puritan is an FDA-registered medical device manufacturer since 1978 and holds ISO and CE Mark certifications.

Products serve diagnostics, forensics and genetics, environmental testing, microbiology media, medical, and controlled environments. Customers include distributors, kit manufacturers, OEM partners, and direct buyers through a new D2C channel. Custom projects typically start at 100,000 units, with NDA-protected development, prototype sampling, and custom bar coding.

Puritan emphasizes USA-made manufacturing, consistent quality, and environmental stewardship — recycling 100% of paper, cardboard, and metal waste. Its differentiation rests on integrated in-house capabilities from formulation to packaging, enabling rapid customization for emerging disease detection and bioterrorism testing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO certified','CE Mark','FDA Medical Device Manufacturer (registered 1978)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Swab manufacturing", "Flocked swab production", "Custom medical device manufacturing", "OEM manufacturing", "Private label manufacturing", "Custom fill (transport media)", "Custom labeling", "Custom packaging", "Custom bar coding", "Kit assembly", "R&D prototyping", "Microbiology media formulation", "Printing", "Labeling systems", "Custom configuration design", "NDA-protected development", "Prototype fabrication", "Artwork and marking design", "Sterile packaging", "Dry transport systems", "Specimen collection device manufacturing", "Single-use medical device manufacturing", "Tongue depressor manufacturing", "Applicator manufacturing"], "industries": ["Diagnostics", "Forensics", "Genetics", "Environmental", "Microbiology Media", "Medical", "Controlled Environments"], "materials": ["Northern white birch", "Polyester flock", "Polystyrene", "Polypropylene", "Cotton", "Wood", "Transport media solutions"], "equipment": ["State-of-the-art print shop", "Labeling systems", "On-site microbiology lab"], "volume": "Custom orders typically start at 100,000 pieces", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Three Maine manufacturing facilities with integrated R&D, microbiology lab, and print shop", "FDA-registered medical device manufacturer since 1978", "Guilford facility powered by 100% renewable energy from wood process waste", "Custom projects supported from prototype to sterile packaging with NDA protection", "100% recycling of paper, cardboard, and metal waste"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1919 as Hardwood Produc