UPDATE companies SET description='QXMedical, LLC was founded in 2007 in Montreal, Canada, on the principle of delivering uncompromised value and quality in underserved, high-growth segments of the medical device market. The company established its Technology and Manufacturing Center in Saint Paul, Minnesota, in 2010, positioning itself in the North American medical device hub. Today, its headquarters are in Roseville, Minnesota. Leadership includes CEO Frank Panarello, who founded electronics manufacturing services provider Trilogix EMS in 1990, and President & Chief Technical Officer Fernando Di Caprio, a serial med-tech founder with over 20 medical device patents.

The company designs and manufactures first-in-class medical devices for minimally invasive coronary, peripheral, and endovascular interventions, as well as emergency and trauma care. Its product portfolio includes balloon catheters, delivery catheters, occlusion balloon catheters, stent graft balloon catheters, embolization particles (such as the i-FLEX line), and guide extensions. Manufacturing occurs at its state-of-the-art facility in Saint Paul, though specific facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not disclosed.

QXMedical serves medical device companies of all sizes, including some of the largest U.S. medical device manufacturers, as well as healthcare professionals and strategic partners. Its devices are used in procedures such as vascular disease treatment, embolization therapy, coronary and peripheral artery disease, and hemorrhage control (including REBOA for trauma care).

The company was started to address unmet needs in complex, minimally invasive procedures, leveraging proprietary technology platforms to deliver unique, high-performance devices with unmatched quality. It emphasizes simplifying complex procedures through innovative, simple solutions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Balloon Catheter", "Delivery Catheter", "Occlusion Balloon Catheter", "Stent Graft Balloon Catheter", "Embolization Particles", "Guide Extension"], "industries": ["Minimally invasive coronary interventions", "Peripheral vascular interventions", "Endovascular interventions", "Emergency and trauma care", "Medical device OEMs"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary technology platforms enabling unique high-performance devices", "State-of-the-art manufacturing facility in the North American medical device hub", "Strategic partnerships with companies of all sizes, including major U.S. medical device OEMs", "Focus on underserved, high-growth segments of the medical device market", "Leadership team with decades of med-tech founding and patent experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 in Montreal, Canada -> /about", "Technology and Manufacturing Center established 2010 in Saint Paul, Minnesota -> /about", "Headquarters in Roseville, Minnesota -> db", "CEO Frank Panarello founded Trilogix EMS in 1990 -> /about", "President & CTO Fernando Di Caprio founded several med-tech companies, holds over 20 patents -> /about", "Director of Business Development London Krueger worked for Medtronic, Boston Scientific, Smith & Nephew -> /about", "ISO 13485 certification -> db", "Capabilities: Balloon Catheter, Delivery Catheter, Occlusion Balloon Catheter, Stent Graft Balloon Catheter, Embolization Particles, Guide Extension -> db", "Products include i-FLEX Embolization Particles -> /", "Serves minimally invasive coronary, peripheral, endovascular interventions -> /"