UPDATE companies SET description='Quantum Plastics, LLC is headquartered in Fort Smith, Arkansas. The company was founded in 2014 as a holding company by Quantum Ventures of Michigan. It operates five manufacturing locations across North America, including divisions in Elgin, Gladewater, Juarez, Raleigh, and Victor.

The company specializes in custom injection molding, blow molding, and assembly. Its processes include gas assist molding, insert molding, two-shot molding, and custom injection molding on presses ranging from 30 to 3,000 tons. Quantum Plastics runs 230 molding presses across its facilities and offers in-house engineering and tooling, integrated product development, assembly and decorating options, and robotic automation. It processes hundreds of resin grades, colorants, and additives per customer specifications.

Quantum Plastics serves the automotive, appliance, medical, food-contact, consumer, and industrial markets. Automotive programs require tight tolerances and structural performance, while blow-molded products such as the Kosmo Cooler and Safe Keeper demonstrate its consumer and industrial reach. The company''s quality systems align with program-specific requirements across these sectors.

Quantum Plastics emphasizes quality engineered into every stage, from tooling design and material handling to process setup and final release. Its approach centers on designing for manufacturability, with tooling and engineering teams evaluating mold design, part geometry, and resin behavior early in development. Certifications including ISO 9001:2015, IATF 16949:2016, ISO 14001:2015, and NSF support controlled processes, traceability, and nonconformance management.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IATF 16949:2016','ISO 14001:2015','NSF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Gas assist molding", "Insert molding", "Custom injection molding", "Two-shot molding", "Blow molding", "Additive and resin processing", "In-house engineering and tooling", "Integrated product development", "Assembly and decorating", "Robotic automation", "First-piece approval", "In-process checks", "Dimensional inspection", "Visual inspection", "Color verification", "Functional testing", "Final-release documentation"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Appliance", "Medical", "Food-contact", "Consumer", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Various resins, colorants, and additives"], "equipment": ["Optiv 443 CMM", "Brown & Sharpe CMM", "Giddings & Lewis-Cordax RS-150 DCC CMM", "Micro-View ST video inspection machine", "Minolta spectrophotometer", "BYK-Gardner spectrophotometer", "X-rite SP 64 Color Spectrometer", "GTI light booth with D65 lighting", "GTI Color matcher-Color Booth", "Hawkeye Gradient Lens Corp VC-35-Borascope", "Tinius Olsen AD987-Extrusion Plastometer", "Mitutoyo comparator", "Micro-Vu comparator", "Presses ranging from 30 to 3,000 tons", "Robotic automation systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house engineering and tooling with design-for-manufacturability focus", "Press capacity from 30 to 3,000 tons across 230 molding presses", "Robotic automation integrated across five manufacturing locations", "Integrated product development from concept through assembly and decorating", "Quality systems certified to ISO 9001:2015, IATF 16949:2016, ISO 14001:2015, and NSF"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Fort Smith, Arkansas -> db", "Founded 2014 as holding company by Quantum Ventures of Michigan -> /", "Five manufacturing locations -> /", "Divisions: Elgin, Gladewater, Juarez, Raleigh, Victor -> /quality", "230 molding presses -> /", "Presses 30-3000 tons -> /", "Processes: gas assist, insert, 2-shot, custom injection, blow molding -> /", "In-house engineering & tooling -> /", "Integrated product development -> /", "Assembly and decorating options -> /", "Robotic automation -> /", "Hundreds of resin grades, colorants, additives -> /", "Industries: automotive, appliance, medical, food-contact, consumer, industrial -> /quality", "Products: Kosmo Cooler, Safe Keeper -> /", "Quality certifications: ISO 9001:2015, IATF 16949:2016, ISO 14001:2015, NSF -> /quality", "Quality equipment: CMMs, spectrophotometers, light booths, borescopes, material testing -> /quality", "300 combined years of experience -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quantum-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rapport, Inc. was founded in 1979 in Golden, Colorado. The company began as a provider of electronic manufacturing services (EMS) and later narrowed its focus to custom cable and wire harness assemblies in 1993.

Today Rapport offers a range of EMS capabilities including custom cable and wire harness fabrication, custom battery pack assembly, and bulk battery distribution. The company employs Kanban and just-in-time (JIT) inventory methods, documented quality procedures with internal and external audit compliance, and structured materials management such as scheduled production releases and safety stock services. Its production lines accommodate both prototype and high-volume runs, though specific facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

The company’s acquisition of Car-Go Battery Company in 2012 expanded its wholesale battery offerings.

Rapport emphasizes cost savings through efficient processes and long-term partnerships. Its stated mission is to act as a strategic manufacturing partner, allowing customers to focus on core competencies while Rapport handles component, battery, and cable assembly needs. The company highlights its use of Kanban and JIT to improve throughput and delivery timelines, as well as its ISO 9001:2015 certification and adherence to UL/CSA and RoHS standards as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic manufacturing services (EMS)", "Custom cable assembly", "Custom wire harness assembly", "Custom battery pack assembly", "Bulk battery distribution", "Kanban inventory management", "Just-in-time (JIT) inventory management", "Documented quality procedures", "Internal and external audit compliance", "Materials management solutions", "Scheduled production releases", "Safety stock services", "Production for prototype and high-volume runs", "Contract electronic manufacturing"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Kanban and Just-in-Time inventory management", "ISO 9001:2015 certification with UL/CSA and RoHS compliance", "Custom cable and wire harness manufacturing since 1993", "Custom battery pack assembly and bulk battery distribution", "Acquisition of Car-Go Battery Company expanding battery offerings"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1979 -> db", "Headquartered in Golden, Colorado -> db", "Providing electronic manufacturing services (EMS) since 1979 -> /", "Focused on custom cable and wire harnesses since 1993 -> /", "Expanded to custom battery packs in 2009 -> /", "Began supplying bulk batteries in 2012 -> /", "Acquired Car-Go Battery Company in March 2012 -> /", "Uses Kanban and Just-in-Time (JIT) inventory methods -> /", "Documented quality procedures with internal and external audit compliance -> /", "Structured materials management including scheduled production releases and safety stock services -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Conforms to customer UL/CSA requirements -> /", "Compliant with RoHS standards -> /", "Production lines ready for small and large runs -> /", "Offers custom battery packs and bulk battery distribution -> /", "Mission to be a strategic manufacturing partner -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rapport-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ready Foods was founded in 1972 by immigrant Luis Abarca in Denver, Colorado. The family-owned company began as a small kitchen on Colfax Avenue, aiming to provide foodservice operators with consistent, scalable recipes. Soon after, the Marco''s product line was launched to offer authentic Mexican cuisine based on Abarca''s heritage. Today, the Abarca family still leads the business, which has expanded into a multi-facility operation.

The company operates as a custom food purveyor and private-label co-packer, producing ready-to-use sauces, soups, salsas, beans, tamales, and tortillas. An in-house R&D team develops custom formulations, and products are packaged in five-pound bags with a six-month frozen shelf life. The workforce numbers around 100 employees.

Ready Foods serves independent and chain restaurants, national and regional accounts, healthcare facilities, educational institutions, caterers, hotels, and event venues. Its products reach customers through major broadline distributors. The company also supports foodservice operators facing labor shortages by providing consistent, ready-to-heat items that reduce prep time.

The founder''s original vision was to solve labor-driven inconsistency in commercial kitchens as diverse cuisines became mainstream. Ready Foods emphasizes a glass-free facility, paperless quality assurance, and BRC-certified food safety. Its mission stresses safe, high-quality food, employee-centered culture, and community impact, while its vision focuses on empowering customers and teams through delicious recipes.', certifications=ARRAY['BRC','AIB','NSF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom contract manufacturing", "Private label co-packing", "Recipe development and scaling", "Sauce and soup production", "Salsa and tortilla production", "Tamale production", "Bean cooking and packaging", "Ready-to-use portioned packaging (5-lb bags)", "Frozen product storage and distribution", "In-house R&D"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Restaurants", "Healthcare", "Education", "Catering", "Hospitality", "Event catering", "Distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1972", "In-house R&D team for custom recipe development and scaling", "Glass-free production facility", "BRC-certified food safety program", "Paperless quality assurance system"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Luis Abarca -> /about-us", "Family-owned, Abarca family at helm -> /about-us", "Headquarters Denver, Colorado -> /about-us, db", "Employee count 100 -> db", "BRC certification -> db, /about-us (2016 timeline)", "AIB audit passed -> /about-us (2005 timeline)", "NSF certified warehouse -> /about-us (2014 timeline)", "Multi-facility production: San Marco''s 8,000 sq ft (1995), Salsa Plant 23,000 sq ft (2000), Bean Plant 33,000 sq ft (2004), Dahlia Plant 80,000 sq ft (2007), 42nd Street Plant 63,000 sq ft (2013) -> /about-us", "Industries served: restaurants, healthcare, education, catering, hotels, events, national/regional accounts -> /about-us", "Capabilities: custom contract manufacturing, private labe