UPDATE companies SET description='Reliance Packaging operates a 160,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Aberdeen, North Carolina, as a member of the Sigma Plastics Group. The Sigma Plastics Group was founded in 1978 by Alfred Teo and has grown into the largest privately owned film extrusion group in North America, with over 40 facilities and an annual throughput exceeding 2 billion pounds of resin. Reliance Packaging functions as a product specialist within this network, focusing on heavy-duty bags and printed films for specific market segments.

The company extrudes, prints, and converts heavy-duty bags and printed roll-stock using five blown extrusion lines, wide-web flexographic presses, and bag-converting equipment. Its extrusion capacity reaches 20 million pounds annually with a maximum web width of 90 inches and roll outer diameters up to 30 inches. Printing is handled by a 52-inch Schiavi six-color press, a 50-inch PCMC INFINITI eight-color press, and a 50-inch inline flexographic press. Converting includes three side-weld bag machines. A turnkey in-house graphic design department supports custom artwork and plate preparation.

Its product line includes mulch and pine bark bags, soil and compost bags, decorative rock bags, play sand and paver base bags, surface-printed and reverse-printed laminated roll stock, food-grade bags and film, freezer-capable ice bags, bailer bags, bags on wickets, industrial bags and films, furniture bags, box and drum liners, and printed industrial shrink film.

The company emphasizes quick turn-around times and quality products, highlighting non-slip ultra-strong film with UV inhibitors and fade-resistant inks designed to perform in tough outdoor conditions. As part of a certified Minority Business Enterprise (NMSDC), Reliance Packaging operates within Sigma Plastics Group''s philosophy of domestic manufacturing, sustainability through the How2Recycle program, and independent facility specialization backed by shared capacity.', certifications=ARRAY['NMSDC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown film extrusion", "Flexographic printing (6-color, 8-color, inline)", "Side-weld bag converting", "Graphic design and prepress", "Roll stock production", "Lamination (reverse printed laminated roll stock)", "Custom film extrusion (up to 90\" width)", "Bag-on-wicket converting", "Shrink film printing"], "industries": ["Lawn and Garden", "Ice-Bag", "Industrial", "Food", "Agricultural"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["52 inch Schiavi 6 Color Flexographic Printing Press", "50 inch PCMC INFINITI 8 color Flexographic Printing Press", "50 inch inline flexo-press", "Three side-weld bag machines", "5 blown extrusion lines (90 inch max width)"], "volume": "20 million pounds annual extrusion capacity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house graphic design department for turnkey artwork support", "Quick turn-around times on custom orders", "Non-slip ultra-strong film with UV inhibitors", "Fade-resistant inks for outdoor durability", "20 million pounds annual extrusion capacity"], "facts_used": ["Location: Aberdeen, NC -> /", "Facility size: 160,000 sq ft -> /", "Sigma Plastics Group founded 1978 by Alfred Teo -> /about", "Sigma Plastics Group: largest privately owned film extrusion group in North America, 40+ facilities, 2B+ lbs annual throughput -> /about", "Extrusion: 5 blown lines, 90\" max width, 20M lbs annual capacity, max roll OD 30\" -> /", "Printing: 52\" Schiavi 6-color, 50\" PCMC INFINITI 8-color, 50\" inline flexo -> /", "Converting: three side-weld bag machines -> /", "In-house graphic design department -> /", "Industries served: Lawn and Garden, Ice-Bag, Industrial -> /", "Products: mulch, pine bark, soil, compost, decorative rock, play sand, paver base bags, surface printed roll stock, reverse printed laminated roll stock, food-grade bags/film, freezer ice bags, bailer bags, bags on wickets, industrial bags/films, furniture bags, box/drum liners, printed shrink film -> /", "Quick turn-around times -> /", "Non-slip ultra strong film with UVI, fade resistant inks -> /", "NMSDC certification (Minority Business Enterprise) -> db, /about", "Sigma Plastics Group philosophy: Made in USA, How2Recycle, independent operation -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='reliance-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Richmond Auto Parts Technology, Inc. (RAPT) operates in Richmond, Kentucky, roughly 36 miles south of Lexington and 10 miles north of Berea. The company was established in 1998 with a $23 million capital investment from its Japanese parent, Aikitec Co., Ltd., and began mass production of automatic transmission gears in July 1999 with an initial team of 20 associates.

RAPT functions as a Tier I and Tier II supplier to the automotive industry, specializing in automatic transmission gears and component parts. The 58-acre campus encompasses a 213,500-square-foot facility staffed by approximately 170 associates. Production capabilities include forging, machining, and assembly for transmissions ranging from 5-speed to 10-speed units, as well as hybrid-electric vehicle (HEV) transmission components. The company has launched programs for 8-speed and 10-speed automatic transmissions and HEV parts.

Primary customers are major Japanese automakers. RAPT has supplied transmission components to Honda since 2000, including 5-speed, 10-speed, and HEV parts, and to Toyota for 8-speed and 10-speed automatic transmissions. The company has received multiple supplier performance awards from both OEMs, including Honda Excellence in Quality and Delivery awards and a Toyota Excellent Quality Performance Award in 2023.

RAPT attributes its differentiation to an associate-centric philosophy summarized in its slogan: “A company that grows strong and survives with associate ideas and knowledge.” The organization emphasizes safety, quality, and production discipline, and maintains ISO 9001:2015 registration. Environmental compliance and community stewardship are also stated priorities.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automatic transmission gear manufacturing", "Forging", "Machining", "Assembly", "Quality inspection and control", "HEV transmission component production", "High-speed transmission manufacturing (5-speed, 8-speed, 10-speed)"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tier I and Tier II supplier to Honda and Toyota", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "213,500 sq ft facility on 58-acre campus with in-house forging", "Associate-driven continuous improvement culture", "Track record of OEM launch programs for 5- to 10-speed and HEV transmissions"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 in Richmond, Kentucky with $23M investment -> /", "Mass production started July 1999 with 20 associates -> /", "Parent company Aikitec Co., Ltd. Japan -> /about", "Facility: 58 acres, 213,500 sq ft, ~170 associates -> /about", "Tier I/II supplier for automatic transmission gears -> /", "Customer launches: Honda (5-speed 2000, 10-speed 2016, HEV 2022/2023), Toyota (8-speed 2022, 10-speed) -> /about", "Awards: Honda Excellence in Quality/Delivery, Toyota Excellent Quality Performance 2023 -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 registered -> /", "Forging expansion noted 2003 -> /about", "Company slogan and associate-centric philosophy -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='richmond-auto-parts-technology-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
